HTTrack known as HTTrack Website Copier is a powerful open-source tool
designed for mirroring websites and downloading their content to a local computer.
This versatile utility offers a user-friendly graphical interface, making it accessible
to users across different operating systems including Windows, Linux and macOS.
With customizable settings users can specify the depth of mirroring, set download
limits and apply filters to tailor the mirroring process to their specific needs. It also
supports incremental updates allowing users to keep mirrored websites
synchronized with changes on the live web. Its web crawling capabilities automate
the process of traversing websites by following links and preserving the relative
structure of the content. Whether for archiving, offline browsing or research
purposes, HTTrack serves as an indispensable tool with extensive documentation
making it suitable for both novice and experienced users. However, users must
exercise ethical and legal considerations when employing it to ensure compliance
with copyright and internet usage laws.
ALGORITHM
Here are the basic steps to use HTTrack:
1.Download and install HTTrack: Visit the official HTTrack website
(https://www.httrack.com/) and download the appropriate version for your operating
system. Install the software on your computer.
2. Launch HTTrack: After installation, launch HTTrack from your computer's
applications or start menu.
3. Create a new project: Click on "Create a new project" or go to "File" > "New" to start
a new project.
4.Set project options: In the project options, we 'll need to provide some basic
information:
• Project name: Choose a name for the project.
• Base path: Select a location on your computer where the downloaded website
will be stored.
• URL: Enter the URL of the website you want to copy.
5. Set filters (optional): If you want to download only specific parts of the website, can set filters. For example, you can exclude certain file types or specific directories.
you
6. Start the download: Click on the "Next" button or go to "Action" > "Download" to
start the downloading process. HTTrack will start crawling the website, following links,
and downloading the necessary files.
7. Monitor the progress: HTTrack will display a progress window showing the number
of files downloaded, their size, and the current status. You can also see the downloaded
files and folders in the chosen base path on your computer.
8. Browse the downloaded website: Once the download is complete, you can open the
downloaded website by navigating to the base path location on your computer and
opening the main HTML file or index.html in a web browser.
